\begin_layout Subsection
Runs on a cluster
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Flex Code
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
hpc/<cluster>/job.*
\end_layout

\end_inset

 run QUICHOTTE in the directory they are submitted from.
 Set 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
EXE
\end_layout

\end_inset

 at the top of the script once:
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Verbatim
cd /scratch/users/$USER/R2G2D
\end_layout

\begin_layout Verbatim
cp ~/QUICHOTTE/examples/helix_4x2_order2/input.dat .
\end_layout

\begin_layout Verbatim
sbatch ~/QUICHOTTE/hpc/create/job.slurm          # CREATE (Slurm)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Verbatim
qsub   ~/QUICHOTTE/hpc/young/job.sge             # Young (SGE)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Verbatim
sbatch $WORK/QUICHOTTE/hpc/archer2/job.slurm  # ARCHER2 (under /work)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The scripts set 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
OMP_NUM_THREADS
\end_layout

\end_inset

 to the allocated cores,
 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1
\end_layout

\end_inset

 (the LAPACK calls already sit inside OpenMP loops) and 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
OMP_STACKSIZE=512M
\end_layout

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Parallelism
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
OpenMP parallelises the loop over energies (Dyson/Keldysh) and the FFT self-energy over site pairs.
 One run uses one node;
 scale 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
OMP_NUM_THREADS
\end_layout

\end_inset

 up to the number of cores.
\end_layout

